:"Føtex","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":55.701464,"lo":12.577651,"d":1409,"h":"07:00-22:00"},{"n":"Spar Nord","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":55.70054,"lo":12.577158,"d":1432,"h":"Mo-Fr 10:00-16:00"},{"n":"Trianglen Central Apotek","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":55.699627,"lo":12.577076,"d":1437,"h":"Mo-Fr 09:00-18:00; Sa 09:00-15:00","w":"https://trianglencentralapotek.dk"},{"n":"Pier47","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.70197,"lo":12.60001,"d":219,"ds":"Pier47 is a DGNB Gold-certified office building located on the Langelinie Pier in Copenhagen, Denmark. It was designed by Lundgaard & Tranberg with inspiration from 19th century warehouses. It is owned by ATP Ejendomme.","wpu":"Pier47","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/%C3%85aljiset_%29Langelinie%3D.jpg/960px-%C3%85aljiset_%29Langelinie%3D.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Amerika Plads","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.6997,"lo":12.5941,"d":371,"ds":"Amerika Plads (lit. \"America Square\") is a public square and surrounding neighbourhood in the Østerbro district of Copenhagen, Denmark. It is the result of a redevelopment of an area in the southern part of the former Freeport of Copenhagen into a mixed-use neighbourhood which consists of dwellings, offices and retail establishments, combining converted historic buildings and modern architecture.","wpu":"Amerika Plads","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Amerika_Plads_-_Frihavnsstationen.jpg/960px-Amerika_Plads_-_Frihavnsstationen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Midtermolen","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.697,"lo":12.5974,"d":371,"ds":"Midtermolen is a pier which extends north from India Quay in the Southern Free Port of Copenhagen, Denmark, dividing the dock into an east and west basin.","wpu":"Midtermolen","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/45/Company_House_Copenhagen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Denmark Expedition Memorial","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.69486,"lo":12.60024,"d":571,"ds":"The Denmark Expedition Memorial is a sculpted boulder at Langelinie in Copenhagen, Denmark, commemorating Ludvig Mylius-Erichsen (1872–1907), Niels Peter Høeg Hagen (1877–1907) and Jørgen Brønlund (1877–1907) who died on the Denmark Expedition to North-East Greenland in 1907. The memorial was unveiled in 1912. It was designed by Kai Nielsen in collaboration with Kaare Klint.","wpu":"Denmark Expedition Memorial","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Denmark_Expedition_Memorial_06.jpg/960px-Denmark_Expedition_Memorial_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Church of the Free Port","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.698889,"lo":12.588611,"d":724,"ds":"The Church of the Free Port (Danish: Frihavnskirken) is a Church of Denmark parish church in the Østerbro district of Copenhagen, Denmark. It was built in 1905 to designs by Thorvald Jørgensen, best known for his design of Christiansborg Palace, home to the Danish Parliament. It takes its name from the Freeport of Copenhagen which had been established on the coast just east of the church a decade earlier.","wpu":"Church of the Free Port","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Frihavnskirken_Copenhagen.jpg/960px-Frihavnskirken_Copenhagen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"The Little Mermaid (statue)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.692861,"lo":12.599278,"d":795,"ds":"The Little Mermaid (Danish: Den lille Havfrue) is a bronze statue by Edvard Eriksen, depicting a mermaid becoming human. The sculpture is displayed on a rock by the waterside at the Langelinie promenade in Copenhagen, Denmark. It is 1.25 metres (4.1 ft) tall and weighs 175 kilograms (385 lb).","wpu":"The Little Mermaid (statue)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7a/Copenhagen_-_the_little_mermaid_statue_-_2013.jpg/960px-Copenhagen_-_the_little_mermaid_statue_-_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Trekroner Fort","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.703056,"lo":12.614444,"d":966,"ds":"Trekroner Søfort (literally Three Crowns Sea Fortress) is a sea fort at the entrance to the Copenhagen harbour. From 1713 until after World War I, Trekroner Fort was part of the fortifications of Copenhagen. The original location of Trekroner Fort was a few hundred meters north of the current one.","wpu":"Trekroner Fort","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Trekroner_%28Copenhagen%29.jpg/960px-Trekroner_%28Copenhagen%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ivar Huitfeldt Column","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.69062,"lo":12.59915,"d":1044,"ds":"The Ivar Huitfeldt Column is a monument at Langelinie in Copenhagen, Denmark, built to commemorate the death of Admiral Ivar Huitfeldt and his men from HDMS Dannebroge, which exploded and sank in the Battle of Køge Bat during the Great Northern War. The monument was constructed in 1886 to a design by Vilhelm Dahlerup.","wpu":"Ivar Huitfeldt Column","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Ivar_Hvitfeldt_Column.jpg/960px-Ivar_Hvitfeldt_Column.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Kastellet, Copenhagen","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.691111,"lo":12.593889,"d":1060,"ds":"Kastellet (Danish pronunciation: [kʰæˈsteˀlð̩]; transl. \"The Citadel\") is a citadel located in Copenhagen, Denmark. It is one of the best preserved fortresses in Northern Europe. It is constructed in the form of a pentagon with bastions at its corners.","wpu":"Kastellet, Copenhagen","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Kastellet_aerial.jpg/960px-Kastellet_aerial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Swedish Gustaf's Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.692222,"lo":12.59,"d":1068,"ds":"Swedish Gustaf's Church (Swedish: Svenska Gustafskyrkan), part of the Church of Sweden Abroad, is the church of the Swedish congregation in Copenhagen, Denmark. It was built between 1907 and 1911 to the design of the Swedish architect Theodor Wåhlin (1864–1948) and is named after King Gustaf V of Sweden.","wpu":"Swedish Gustaf's Church","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/55/Nordenskirker_Gustaf%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Garrison Cemetery, Copenhagen","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.695,"lo":12.583889,"d":1152,"ds":"Garrison Cemetery (Danish: Garnisons Kirkegård) is a cemetery in Copenhagen, Denmark. It was inaugurated in 1671 on a site just outside the Eastern City Gate, as a military cemetery complementing the naval Holmens Cemetery which had been inaugurated a few years earlier on a neighbouring site. Later the cemetery was opened to civilian burials as well.","wpu":"Garrison Cemetery, Copenhagen","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Garnisons_Kirkeg%C3%A5rd_06.jpg/960px-Garnisons_Kirkeg%C3%A5rd_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Memorial to Nordic Volunteers and Fallen","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.69141,"lo":12.58954,"d":1158,"ds":"The Memorial to Nordic Volunteers and Fallen (Danish: Mindesmærke for Frivillige og Faldne), located on Smedelinien, part of Kastellet, is a memorial to 28 Norwegian, Swedish and Finnish volunteers of the First (1848–50) and Second Schleswig War (1864). It was inaugurated in 1920 to design by Anders Bundgaard.","wpu":"Memorial to Nordic Volunteers and Fallen","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Mindesm%C3%A6rke_for_frivillige_og_faldne.jpg/960px-Mindesm%C3%A6rke_for_frivillige_og_faldne.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Gefion Fountain","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.689444,"lo":12.5975,"d":1184,"ds":"The Gefion Fountain (Danish: Gefionspringvandet) is a large fountain on the harbour front in Copenhagen, Denmark. It features a large-scale group of oxen pulling a plow and being driven by the Norse goddess Gefjon. It is located in Nordre Toldbod area next to Kastellet and immediately south of Langelinie.","wpu":"Gefion Fountain","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Gefion_Fountain%2C_Copenhagen%2C_Copenhagen.jpg/960px-Gefion_Fountain%2C_Copenhagen%2C_Copenhagen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Oslo Plads","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.6923,"lo":12.5867,"d":1194,"ds":"Oslo Plads (\"Oslo Square\") is a public square in the Østerbro area of Copenhagen, Denmark. The square received its name in 1962. Before then, the square was part of the street Østerbrogade.","wpu":"Oslo Plads","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Oslo_Plads.jpg/960px-Oslo_Plads.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Victor Borges Plads","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.7016,"lo":12.5808,"d":1216,"ds":"Victor Borges Plads is a public square in the Østerbro district of Copenhagen, Denmark.","wpu":"Victor Borges Plads","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Victor_Borges_Plads.jpg/960px-Victor_Borges_Plads.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"B&W Hallerne","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.693056,"lo":12.616667,"d":1298,"ds":"B&W Hallerne (English: The B&W Halls) is a former industrial complex located on the island of Refshaleøen in Copenhagen, Denmark. Built in the early 1960s by Burmeister & Wain, the complex consists of two large halls which were used to build ships until 1996. Currently, the facilities are used for culture and entertainment activities.","wpu":"B&W Hallerne","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Eurovision_Song_Contest_Refshaleoen_Copenhagen_20140506_001_%2814121539601%29.jpg/960px-Eurovision_Song_Contest_Refshaleoen_Copenhagen_20140506_001_%2814121539601%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Mastekranen","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.6881,"lo":12.606,"d":1375,"ds":"Mastekranen (English: The Masting Crane) is an 18th-century masting sheer and present landmark on Holmen in Copenhagen, Denmark. It was designed by architect Philip de Lange and built in 1748–51 as part of the Royal Naval Shipyard at Holmen.","wpu":"Mastekranen","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Mastekranen_Holmen.jpg/960px-Mastekranen_Holmen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Trianglen, Copenhagen","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":55.699167,"lo":12.577222,"d":1430,"ds":"Trianglen (lit. 'The Triangle') is a central junction and public space in the Østerbro district of Copenhagen, Denmark. Five streets meet in the junction: Blegdamsvej, Øster Allé, Østerbrogade, Nordre Frihavnsgade and Odensegade. Trianglen is a station on the City Circle Line of the Copenhagen Metro.","wpu":"Trianglen, Copenhagen","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/P.v._jensen-klint_15%2C_tramway_waiting-room_1904-1907_cropped.jpg/960px-P.v._jensen-klint_15%2C_tramway_waiting-room_1904-1907_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Copenhagen (Danish: København [kʰøpm̩ˈhɑwˀn] ) is the capital and most populous city of Denmark, with an urban population of 1.4 million. The city is situated mainly on the island of Zealand (Sjælland), with a smaller part on the island of Amager. Copenhagen is separated from Malmö, Sweden, by the Øresund strait.","wpu":"Copenhagen","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/2018_-_Christiansborg_from_the_Marble_Bridge.jpg/960px-2018_-_Christiansborg_from_the_Marble_Bridge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}